; Force `pnpm -r <script>` to run one workspace package at a time.
; packages/sim's E2E soak tests (Task 12) run 5-10 real virtual AGVs +
; an in-process MQTT broker + orchestrator for several minutes of real
; wall-clock time in a single Node process. Under pnpm's default
; concurrent-workspace execution, that CPU/event-loop pressure was found
; to destabilize an unrelated, otherwise-100%-passing upstream timing
; race in packages/robot-interface's vda-5050-lib-based tests (an
; "AgvController: Client is not started" unhandled rejection from a
; stray internal publish timer firing after controller.stop() — a
; pre-existing library quirk, not something introduced by Task 12) when
; run at the same time via plain `corepack pnpm -r test`. Serializing
; workspace script execution removes the resource contention without
; touching any package's own test code. See task-12-report.md for the
; full investigation.
workspace-concurrency=1
